      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xasu__mlkem__common__apis_1ga0699c83a7c9436b39a0c8d2d6b9cfcf6" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>s32</type>
        <definition>s32 XAsu_MlkemValidateParams</definition>
        <argsstring>(const XAsu_MlkemEncapsDecapsParams *MlkemParamsPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_MlkemValidateParams</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mlkem_encaps_decaps_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MlkemEncapsDecapsParams</ref> *</type>
          <declname>MlkemParamsPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function validates the ML-KEM encapsulation/decapsulation parameters. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MlkemParamsPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mlkem_encaps_decaps_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MlkemEncapsDecapsParams</ref> structure which holds the ML-KEM encapsulation/decapsulation parameters.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if validation of ML-KEM parameters is successful.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if any argument is invalid. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate ML-KEM params pointer.</para><para>Validate the parameter set against the FIPS 203 approved sets.</para><para>Validate ciphertext address, which is the output for encaps and the input for decaps.</para><para>Validate the shared secret address and buffer length, which is an output of both operations and is 32 bytes for every parameter set.</para><para>Validate that exactly one of KeyAddr or KeyId is provided, and that a vault sourced key carries no length.</para>        </inbodydescription>
